  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Resilience through Dialogue and Art (CORDIAL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cote d&apos;Ivoire):  In response to the country&apos;s history of violence during key political events, such as elections, USAID/C&amp;ocirc;te d&apos;Ivoire is implementing an activity to foster reconciliation in areas affected by political violence originating from the 2020 presidential electoral cycle.  With FY 2024 funds, the Community Resilience through Dialogue and Art (CORDIAL) activity will work alongside select communities to prevent future political violence and promote reconciliation in the lead-up to, during, and after the 2025/2026 presidential and legislative elections.  USAID will provide trauma healing support to victims through cognitive behavior therapy tools and art (i.e. music, theater, and painting) at the community level.  It will facilitate dialogue and reconciliation through civil society, allowing opposing groups to voice their grievances and find a middle ground.  The activity also will bring together community members from various ethnic groups and political affiliations through joint cultural and artistic events to promote social cohesion and prevent the onset of violence at the community-level. .By promoting social cohesion in the lead-up to the 2025 presidential election, this activity will support the Integrated Country Strategy (ICS) Mission Objective 1.2: C&amp;ocirc;te d&apos;Ivoire promotes social cohesion and respect for human rights...</narrative>
  </description>
